.TH MINITUN 1 "2026-08-01" "MiniTun 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minitun \- manage MiniTun servers and TCP tunnels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minitun
.RI [ --socket " path" ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minitun
is a stateless command-line client. It sends one request to the local
.BR minitund (8)
Unix socket, prints the response, and exits. It never opens the MiniTun SQLite
databases or connects directly to a public server.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "server add " endpoint " [--name " name "]"
Add a public MiniTun server.
.TP
.BI "server login " server " [--token-stdin]"
Store a Token for a server. Without
.BR --token-stdin ,
the Token is read from a terminal with echo disabled.
.TP
.B server list [--json]
List configured servers.
.TP
.BI "server inspect " server " [--json]"
Inspect one server by ID or name.
.TP
.BI "server remove " server
Remove one server and its tunnels.
.TP
.BI "tun add " server " " local-port " " server-port " [--local-host " host "] [--name " name "]"
Create a TCP tunnel. The default local host is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BI "tun list [" server "] [--json]"
List all tunnels or the tunnels for one server.
.TP
.BI "tun inspect " tunnel " [--json]"
Inspect one tunnel by ID or name.
.TP
.BI "tun remove " tunnel
Remove one tunnel.
.TP
.B status
Show aggregate client state.
.TP
.B daemon status
Check the local daemon.
.TP
.B version
Print version, commit, build, compiler, and protocol information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " path"
Use a local socket other than /run/minitun/minitun.sock.
.TP
.B --json
Emit stable JSON for supported list and inspect commands.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success; 2 invalid arguments; 3 daemon unavailable;
4 authentication failure; 5 remote or network failure; and 10 protocol,
database, resource, or internal failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/minitun/minitun.sock
Local daemon control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR minitund (8),
.BR minitun-server (8)
